"In the small life of someone,\n'should've known my place in it,\nLike an even smaller tardigrade,\nWas I always lurking in it.\n\nMight've been an interesting one,\nLike the tardigrade is for us,\nBut nothing more than a subject of use,\nShould've known my stand in the gus'.\n\nAttachment is a human nature,\nThe intensity though vary a lot!\nA truthful podcast, what I always wanted,\nInstead of a buttering bot.\n\nKeeping me, at the top of the list,\nYes, they were always pretending,\nThe tardigrade, always being a micro matter,\nAnd the lies? Were still descending.\n\nThe show of care,\nAfter one truthful podcast,\nThough I know, it won't be for long,\nAs for the tardigrade to be noticed, their list's vast!"